# InkDeck secret transport — copy to `.env`, fill in, then push over USB:
#
#   adb push .env /sdcard/Android/data/dev.inkdeck/files/import/
#
# The app reads each KEY=value into the encrypted vault and shreds this file on arrival.
# It is a transport, not storage — `.env` is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# VAULT_PASSPHRASE is deliberately refused on import. A passphrase sitting in plaintext beside
# the vault it opens protects nothing; if you do not want to type one, leave the passphrase
# toggle off (the default) instead of writing it down here.

# This file IS committed — it is the template. Put real values in `.env`, never here.

TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# Optional. Setting it here counts as a pre-pairing: the bot will accept that chat immediately
# and you never type the 6-digit code on the panel. Leave blank to pair from the app instead.
# It is also the allowlist — every other chat is ignored silently.
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
FINNHUB_API_KEY=

# Host definitions for the terminal, until the host editor exists (Plan.md §4.2).
# Format: SSH_HOST_<alias> = user@host:port key=<key-name-in-vault> strict=<yes|ask|no>
# SSH_HOST_myserver=user@example.com:22 key=id_ed25519 strict=ask
